  "prediction": "**CBS News Overhauls \"The Early Show\" with New Team**\n\nIn a bid to boost ratings, CBS News has made significant changes to its morning program, \"The Early Show.\" The show's co-hosts, Harry Smith and Maggie Rodriguez, along with weather forecaster Dave Price, have been replaced by a new team.\n\n**New Team Members**\n\nChris Wragge and Erica Hill, who have been co-anchors of the Saturday edition of \"The Early Show\" since 2008, will take over as co-anchors of the weekday show starting January 3. Jeff Glor, who has been anchoring the network's Saturday newscast, will join the team as a regular news reader. Marysol Castro, a former weather anchor for ABC's \"Good Morning America\" weekend edition, will serve as the new weather anchor.\n\n**Changes for Departing Hosts**\n\nHarry Smith, who had the longest tenure on the show, will remain at CBS News but will take on a new role as the primary substitute anchor for Katie Couric's evening newscast, \"Face the Nation,\" and \"Sunday Morning.\" Maggie Rodriguez and Dave Price will be discussing future roles at the network.\n\n**Ratings Expectations**\n\nCBS News President Sean McManus expressed confidence in the new team, stating that he believes they will \"grow\" the show. However, the network is not expecting immediate ratings changes, given that NBC's \"Today\" show has consistently ranked first in the morning news ratings.\n\n**Industry Reaction**\n\nVeteran television critic David Bianculli praised CBS News for shaking things up, but noted that the suddenness of the changes was surprising. He added that it's \"hard to fault\" the network for trying to boost ratings.\n\nThe changes are part of a larger effort by CBS News to revamp its morning program and compete with other networks in the ratings. Only time will tell if the new team will be able to break the show out of third place.",
